From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deepti Jaggi <quic_djaggi@quicinc.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Dec 2024 16:13:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: nord: add reg-names to cpucp mbox node

The restructured qcom-cpucp-mbox driver looks up its tx/rx register
regions by name via platform_get_resource_byname(), replacing the old
index-based devm_of_iomap() lookup. Add the matching reg-names
property to the Nord pdp0_mbox node so it continues to probe
correctly with the new driver.

The ordering matches the existing reg array: index 0
(0x17610000) is the rx region, index 1 (0x19980000) is the tx
region.

Signed-off-by: Deepti Jaggi <quic_djaggi@quicinc.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord.dtsi
index 5e1a35479480..480371a0c398 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord.dtsi
@@ -2575,6 +2575,7 @@ pdp0_mbox: mailbox@17610000 {
 				     "qcom,x1e80100-cpucp-mbox";
 			reg = <0x0 0x17610000 0x0 0x4c08>,
 			      <0x0 0x19980000 0x0 0x300>;
+			reg-names = "rx", "tx";
 			#mbox-cells = <1>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 56 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		};
--
2.34.1
